{"SurveyID":"SV_bynxxD5ddXRJNhc","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID801","SecondaryAttribute":"Flooding Valleys Four towns are located in the valleys of the Whitgus mountains. During the sprin...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Flooding Valleys<\/b><br><br>\n\n\nFour towns are located in the valleys of the Whitgus mountains. During the spring snow melt, the valleys are protected from floods by a system of dams that are badly maintained. One day, the dams protecting the Leefside and Llyne valleys collapse. If nothing is done, then the Leefside and Llyne valleys will be flooded and the inhabitants will die.  The remaining dams have manually operated floodgates. The governor of the mountain district can airlift an operator to open the floodgates, which would redirect the water to other valleys. However, there is only one high altitude helicopter available, so only one dam can be reached in time. This leaves the governor with two options:\n<br><br>\n\n<ul>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option1<\/i>:\nAirlift the operator to redirect the flood heading towards Leefside Valley to Frostford Valley. This would kill 200 people in the Frostford Valley but save 300 people in the Leefside Valley.\n\n<\/li>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option2<\/i>:\nAirlift the operator to redirect the flood heading towards Llyne Valley to Bleakburn Valley. This would kill 600 people in the Bleakburn Valley but save 750 people in the Llyne Valley.\n\n<\/li>\n\n<\/ul><br<br><br>\n\n\nIf you were faced with this choice, would you choose option 1 or option 2?\n<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.valleysFlooding.moral.comparisonType.ratio_vs_utility_1.5utility_3xvictims.n_saved1.300.n_saved2.750.n_total1.500.n_total2.1350.n_victims1.200.n_victims2.600.high_ratio_first","QuestionID":"QID801","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Flooding Valleys Four towns are located in the valleys of the Whitgus mountains. During the sprin...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1: Defi