{"SurveyID":"SV_bynxxD5ddXRJNhc","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1017","SecondaryAttribute":"Flooding Valleys Four towns containing papermills are located in the valleys of the Whitgus mount...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Flooding Valleys<\/b><br><br>\n\n\nFour towns containing papermills are located in the valleys of the Whitgus mountains. During the spring snow melt, the valleys are protected from floods by a system of dams that are badly maintained. One day, the dams protecting the Leefside and Llyne valleys collapse. If nothing is done, then the papermills in Leefside and Llyn valleys will be flooded and the paper rolls waiting for shipment will be destroyed by the water. The remaining dams have manually operated floodgates. The governor of the mountain district can airlift an operator to open the floodgates, which would redirect the water to other valleys. However, there is only one high altitude helicopter available, so only one dam can be reached in time. This leaves the governor with two options:\n<br><br>\n\n<ul>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option1<\/i>:\nAirlift the operator to redirect the flood heading towards Leefside Valley to Frostford Valley. This will destroy 200 paper rolls in Frostford Valley, but save 400  paper rolls in Leefside Valley.\n\n<\/li>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option2<\/i>:\nAirlift the operator to redirect the flood heading towards Llyne Valley to Bleackburn Valley. This will destroy 600 paper rolls in Bleackburn valley, but save 900 paper rolls in Llyne Valley.\n\n<\/li>\n\n<\/ul><br<br><br>\n\n\nIf you were faced with this choice, would you choose option 1 or option 2?\n<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.valleysFlooding.econ.comparisonType.ratio_vs_utility_1.5utility_3xvictims.n_saved1.400.n_saved2.900.n_total1.600.n_total2.1500.n_victims1.200.n_victims2.600.high_ratio_first","QuestionID":"QID1017","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Flooding Valleys Four towns containing paperm