{"SurveyID":"SV_bynxxD5ddXRJNhc","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1025","SecondaryAttribute":"Fuming Hospital In a hospital complex with buildings of different sizes, there are deadly corrosi...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Fuming Hospital<\/b><br><br>\n\n\nIn a hospital complex with buildings of different sizes, there are deadly corrosive fumes rising through the central ventilation system due to an accident in one of the laboratories in the middle of the night. The corrosive fumes were found in two separate vents heading towards the Evergreen and Clearview buildings, respectively. If nothing is done, then the Evergreen and Clearview buildings will be exposed to the deadly fumes. These buildings house patients of the hospital complex. <br>\nThe control engineer can redirect one of the fumes by running to a junction in the ventilation system and opening and closing specific vents, but there is not enough time to redirect both fumes. This leaves the engineer with two options:\n<br><br>\n\n<ul>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option1<\/i>:\nRedirect the fumes heading towards the Clearview building to the Summer Stone building. This would kill the 600 patients in the Summer Stone building but save the 900 patients in the Clearview building.\n\n<\/li>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option2<\/i>:\nRedirect the fumes heading towards the Evergreen building to the Harmony Grove building,. This would kill the 200 patients in the Harmony Grove but save the 400 patients in the Evergreen building.\n\n<\/li>\n\n<\/ul><br<br><br>\n\n\nIf you were faced with this choice, would you choose option 1 or option 2?\n<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.fumingHospital.moral.comparisonType.ratio_vs_utility_1.5utility_3xvictims.n_saved1.400.n_saved2.900.n_total1.600.n_total2.1500.n_victims1.200.n_victims2.600.high_ratio_second","QuestionID":"QID1025","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Fuming Hospital In a hospital complex with buildings of different