{"SurveyID":"SV_bynxxD5ddXRJNhc","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID811","SecondaryAttribute":"Hopsital Power Outage During a city-wide power outage, the local hospital needs to rely on backup...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Hopsital Power Outage<\/b><br><br>\n\n\nDuring a city-wide power outage, the local hospital needs to rely on backup generators to keep patients on life support alive. The only electrical engineer on site receives a warning that the generators for the Spring Forest and East Valley buildings are overheating and will lose power in the next 5 minutes. The engineer has just enough time to run to a switching station to replace the failing generators with power destined to other buildings. This leaves the engineer with two options:\n<br><br>\n\n<ul>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option1<\/i>:\nUse the generator for the Highland building to keep the Spring Forest building powered. This would kill 20 patients in the Highland building but save 30 patients in the Spring Forest building.\n\n<\/li>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option2<\/i>:\nUse the generator for the Hopedale building to keep the East Valley building powered. This would kill 60 patients in the Hopedale building but save 75 patients in the East Valley building.\n\n<\/li>\n\n<\/ul><br<br><br>\n\n\nIf you were faced with this choice, would you choose option 1 or option 2?\n<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.powerHospital.moral.comparisonType.ratio_vs_utility_1.5utility_3xvictims.n_saved1.30.n_saved2.75.n_total1.50.n_total2.135.n_victims1.20.n_victims2.60.high_ratio_first","QuestionID":"QID811","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Hopsital Power Outage During a city-wide power outage, the local hospital needs to rely on backup...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1: Definitely Option 1"},"2":{"Display":"2"},"3":{"Display":"3"},"4":{"Display":"4"},"5":{"Display":"5"},"6":{"Display":"6: Definitely Option 2"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6"],"Validation"