{"SurveyID":"SV_bynxxD5ddXRJNhc","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID924","SecondaryAttribute":"Human Sacrifice For his imperial cult, the king Chirfiqa demands in-kind tribute in the form of s...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Human Sacrifice<\/b><br><br>\n\n\nFor his imperial cult, the king Chirfiqa demands in-kind tribute in the form of sheep once a year. He typically confiscates all sheep in two villages, but if enough sheep are brought to the capital voluntarily, a village is spared. This year, the villages Fiorn and Liory are chosen to provide the tribute.<br>\nAn intelligence officer who is abhorred by heavy tribute demands by the king has detected a group of villagers from a group of villagers from each village who have fled in an attempt to hide their sheep. Should they be able to hide their sheep would survive. The officer can follow the tracks of the escaped villagers in order to confiscate their sheep, however given the time constraints only one of the two groups can be pursued. This leaves the officer with two options:\n<br><br>\n\n<ul>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option1<\/i>:\nConfiscate the sheep from the villagers fleeing Fiorn. This would kill the 100 escaped sheep but save the 400 sheep in Fiorn.\n\n<\/li>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option2<\/i>:\nConfiscate the sheep from the villagers fleeing Liory. This would kill the 300 escaped sheep but save the 750 sheep in Liory.\n\n<\/li>\n\n<\/ul><br<br><br>\n\n\nIf you were faced with this choice, would you choose option 1 or option 2?\n<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.sacrificeHuman.econ.comparisonType.ratio_vs_utility_1.5utility_3xvictims.n_saved1.400.n_saved2.750.n_total1.500.n_total2.1050.n_victims1.100.n_victims2.300.high_ratio_first","QuestionID":"QID924","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Human Sacrifice For his imperial cult, the king Chirfiqa demands in-kind tribute in the form of s...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1: Definitely Option 1"},"2":{"Dis