{"SurveyID":"SV_bynxxD5ddXRJNhc","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID744","SecondaryAttribute":"Human Sacrifice For his imperial cult, the king of the Chirfiqa demands human sacrifices once a y...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Human Sacrifice<\/b><br><br>\n\n\nFor his imperial cult, the king of the Chirfiqa demands human sacrifices once a year. He typically burns two villages to the ground and kills all its residents, but if enough volunteers are sacrificed in the capital, a village is spared. This year, the villages Fiorn and Liory are chosen to provide the sacrifice. <br>\nAn intelligence officer who is abhorred by the prospect of burning down villages has detected a group of villagers from each village who have fled in an attempt to hide in the capital. Should they arrive at the capital they would survive. The officer can follow the tracks of the escaped villagers in order to detain them, however given the time constraints only one of the two groups can be detained. This leaves the officer with two options:\n<br><br>\n\n<ul>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option1<\/i>:\nDetain the villagers fleeing Fiorn. This would kill the 20 escapees but save the 40 residents of Fiorn.\n\n<\/li>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option2<\/i>:\nDetain the villagers fleeing from Liory. This would kill the 60 escapees but save the 90 residents of Liory.\n\n<\/li>\n\n<\/ul><br<br><br>\n\n\nIf you were faced with this choice, would you choose option 1 or option 2?\n<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.sacrificeHuman.moral.comparisonType.ratio_vs_utility_1.5utility_3xvictims.n_saved1.40.n_saved2.90.n_total1.60.n_total2.150.n_victims1.20.n_victims2.60.high_ratio_first","QuestionID":"QID744","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Human Sacrifice For his imperial cult, the king of the Chirfiqa demands human sacrifices once a y...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1: Definitely Option 1"},"2":{"Display":"2"},"3":{"Display":"3"},"4":{"Display":"4"},"5":{"Display"