{"SurveyID":"SV_bynxxD5ddXRJNhc","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1040","SecondaryAttribute":"Space Supplies In the year 3050, humans have colonized multiple planets. However, they still rely...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Space Supplies<\/b><br><br>\n\n\nIn the year 3050, humans have colonized multiple planets. However, they still rely on oxygen tanks which are periodically shipped from Earth. <br>\nOne day, the transporters destined for the planets Phithitis and Reawei explode en route, leaving these planets without oxygen. If nothing is done, the populations of Phithitis and Reawei will die as a result. <br>\nThe planets Otroa and Hurilia have just received their oxygen shipments, but the shipments have not been distributed yet, and the transporters need extensive maintenance before their next mission. However, in a nearby space station, there is a fast transporter that could reach these planets in time to pick up their oxygen and ferry it to Phithitis or Reawei. This leaves the space agency with two options:\n<br><br>\n\n<ul>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option1<\/i>:\nOrder the fast transporter to pick up the oxygen from Hurilia and to ship it to Reawei. This would kill the 60 citizens on Hurilia but will save the 75 citizens on Reawei.\n\n<\/li>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option2<\/i>:\nOrder the fast transporter to pick up the oxygen from Otrao and to ship it to Phithitis. This would kill the 20 citizens on Otroa but will save the 30 citizens on Phithitis.\n\n<\/li>\n\n<\/ul><br<br><br>\n\n\nIf you were faced with this choice, would you choose option 1 or option 2?\n<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.suppliesSpace.moral.comparisonType.ratio_vs_utility_1.5utility_3xvictims.n_saved1.30.n_saved2.75.n_total1.50.n_total2.135.n_victims1.20.n_victims2.60.high_ratio_second","QuestionID":"QID1040","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Space Supplies In the year 3050, humans have colonized multiple planets. However, they 